+
+## Complete `.env.local` Template (for local development)
+
+Create this file at the repo root as `.env.local` (never commit):
+
+```env
+# Required
+NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
+NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGci...
+SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGci...
+NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
+
+# Email
+RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
+EMAIL_FROM=MathPivot <noreply@mathpivot.com>
+
+# Stripe (test keys for local dev)
+STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
+NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
+STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
+
+# AI Math Tutor
+ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
+
+# Monitoring
+NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://...@sentry.io/...
+SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=sntrys_...
+
+# Google (optional)
+GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com
+GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-...
+```
+
+---
+
+## Vercel Environment Variable Checklist
+
+Copy this into your Vercel project:
+
+- [ ] `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` (Production, Preview, Development)
+- [ ] `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (Production, Preview, Development)
+- [ ] `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (Production, Preview) — **do not add to Development**
+- [ ] `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` (per-environment; `https://mathpivot.com` for production)
+- [ ] `RESEND_API_KEY` (Production, Preview)
+- [ ] `EMAIL_FROM` (Production, Preview)
+- [ ] `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` (Production=live key, Preview=test key)
+- [ ] `NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (matching production/test keys)
+- [ ] `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (matching production/test webhooks)
+- [ ] `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (Production, Preview)
+- [ ] `NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN` (Production)
+- [ ] `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN` (Production build only)
+
+---
+
+## Supabase Post-Setup
+
+### Run migrations
+
+If setting up a new Supabase project, run all SQL files in `supabase/migrations/` in order (00001 through 00047) in Supabase SQL Editor.
+
+### Verify RLS is enabled
+
+In Supabase → Authentication → Policies, confirm every table has Row Level Security **enabled**. Every migration adds the appropriate policies.
+
+### Configure Auth
+
+Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration:
+- **Site URL:** `https://mathpivot.com`
+- **Redirect URLs:** add `https://mathpivot.com/auth/callback`, `https://mathpivot.com/auth/confirm`, `https://mathpivot.com/**` (and your preview URLs)
+
+### Create initial admin account
+
+After first deploy, sign up normally, then in SQL Editor:
+
+```sql
+UPDATE users_profile
+SET role = 'super_admin'
+WHERE email = 'your-admin@email.com';
+```
+
+---
+
+## Deploy Order (First Time)
+
+1. Create Supabase project → run all migrations → configure auth URLs
+2. Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in Vercel
+3. Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` in Vercel
+4. Deploy Vercel → verify site loads
+5. Verify Resend domain → set `RESEND_API_KEY`, `EMAIL_FROM` → redeploy
+6. Sign up, promote to super_admin via SQL
+7. Test lead capture (public forms), verify email arrives
+8. Add Stripe (test mode) → configure webhook → test purchase
+9. Add remaining optional services (Anthropic, Sentry, Google) as needed
+10. Switch Stripe to live mode when ready to accept real payments
+
+---
+
+## Verification Commands
+
+After each env var change and redeploy:
+
+```bash
+# Test the /api/health endpoint
+curl https://mathpivot.com/api/health
+
+# Should return: {"status":"ok","supabase":"connected"}
+```
+
+If Supabase is misconfigured, this will fail with a clear error.
